{
  "$defs": {
    "ReminderWindow": {
      "description": "A precise \"from X to Y\" the six-bucket ENUM cannot express.",
      "properties": {
        "start_minute": {
          "maximum": 1439,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Start Minute",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "end_minute": {
          "maximum": 1439,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "End Minute",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "start_minute",
        "end_minute"
      ],
      "title": "ReminderWindow",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Supporter": {
      "description": "One person the subject can realistically do something with.\n\n`relation` is free text, not the six-value ENUM `user_profile` uses: the\npoint of the extension table is that \"室友\" and \"教练\" are real answers.\nThe legacy columns mirror the first two positions; an unsupported custom\nrelation projects to NULL but remains intact in the canonical list.",
      "properties": {
        "relation": {
          "maxLength": 32,
          "minLength": 1,
          "title": "Relation",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "nickname": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "maxLength": 64,
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Nickname"
        },
        "influence": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "enum": [
                "弱",
                "中",
                "强"
              ],
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Influence"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "relation"
      ],
      "title": "Supporter",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "description": "PATCH /api/profile. Omitted fields are left alone; null clears one.\n\nThe distinction matters: a form that only edits one section must not wipe\nthe others. The handler applies `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`, so\n\"absent\" and \"explicitly set to null\" are genuinely different requests —\nthe first is a no-op for that column, the second empties it.\n\nDeliberately *not* here: `current_module`, `module1_done_flag`,\n`risk_level`, `expression_style`. The first two are programme state the\nrouter owns, and letting a subject POST their own `current_module` would\nlet them skip the gating that module 1 exists to enforce. The last two are\nassessments *about* someone, not statements *by* them.",
  "properties": {
    "nickname": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "maxLength": 58,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Nickname"
    },
    "tag": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "maxLength": 5,
          "minLength": 5,
          "pattern": "^[0-9]{5}$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Tag"
    },
    "age": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "maximum": 120,
          "minimum": 10,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
